<description>&lt;p&gt;Armed groups continue ambushing civilians, with killings reported in Jebel Boma County and a road ambush in Warrap County, while security forces seized a truckload of alcohol in Mundri West as part of a substance-abuse crackdown. A Christian woman was killed for refusing a forced marriage to a Muslim man and two pastors were wounded in a separate attack, prompting women in Greater Mundri to demand protection. In Kapoeta South, two youth were killed after a SSPDF arrest, the Kapoeta South Commissioner confirmed the killing of an SPLM secretary and a friend, and a veteran journalist was buried in Juba. The Ministry of Gender and stakeholders reviewed draft guidelines for safe houses for GBV survivors. Two battle-related deaths were recorded in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://reliefweb.int/report/south-sudan/accountability-affected-populations-aap-working-group-south-sudan-meeting-minutes-25-may-2026&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb (OCHA)&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://reliefweb.int/report/central-african-republic/central-african-republic-situation-report-no-94-17-november-2026&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb (OCHA)&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://reliefweb.int/report/central-african-republic/republique-centrafricaine-rapport-de-situation-ndeg-94-au-17-novembre-2026&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb (OCHA)&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://reliefweb.int/report/sudan/sudan-population-movements-sudan-16-november-2026&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb (OCHA)&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;OkayAfrica&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Social News XYZ&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisgFBVV95cUxPeExHSlFyZkVkaVItZVRMaW1nM2hHSkdvMUNjdV9yRUo0UHBFY01qNTRweGRuRVlEVjJ1bXd3ZWQ2ek05MmZhUjFaaFBoejVTc09XWWstSC1DQl9vRzdJRThFWjh4cTBhaXdMZkxtcl9LR0tqaTBIcDRmS